A||||11||DR650SE||New amp. Is it a crappy one?||||9||
Z||000000||DR650SE||11-07-2001||12:50 AM||||I Just got an amp from murrays auto parts store.  It is a Rampage by Audiovox.   It is 100 watts.  I walnt to use it to push a 10" sub.  I'd somehow like to put the sub under the dash.  bayme up and under??  If not then maybe in the weel well.  I don't want to take up leg room.  My question is did I waste $40 on this amp?  Is it enough?  I'm not looking for blow your head off bass.  Just some vibration maybe.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||9
Z||000001||DR650SE||11-07-2001||12:53 AM||||Also, What size box do I need.  I read the thread about of a box can effect proformance.  What If I didn't use a box?  Will a Small box do?  I'm nerw to the sub division.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000002||U Wanna Race||11-07-2001||01:48 AM||||To power a 10 inch sub you will need more than a 100 watt amp.  You will want to look at the sub you want to buy and find out how many watts and ohms it requires.  Then find an amp that will suite the requirements.  If you just want some rumble then you might look into buying a good pair of 3-way speakers.  Like rockford fosgate, cerwin vega or something to that affect.  And you said you got an audiovox amp.  Audiovox is a generic brand, you might want to stray away from buying such brands in the future.  With generic amps there are problems such as overheating, short life span, and overall poor sound quality.  Do yourself a favor and checkout <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com" TARGET=_blank>www.crutchfield.com</A>  they have a lot of information and product reviews.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GodSend||11-07-2001||09:24 AM||||100watts is more then enough for a single 10".  In order to double the volume of a sub (add +3dbs) you will need a significant amount more wattage, and therefore is not worth it (read : getting a 150 watt amp will do very little).<P>*BUT*<P>Consider that the amp you just purchased is VERY low end (sorry).  It may do the job (hard to say).  But I would wager that upgrading to a 100 watt amp of a better brand will make all the difference (Look for Pheonix Gold, Fosgate, Soundstream, and those kinds).<P>  There are several brands of amps which are very afforadable yet provide adequate quality (MTX comes to mind).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DR650SE||11-07-2001||01:45 PM||||Crap.  Anyone want a the amp?  $30+shipping.  ||||reg||8
Z||000005||GodSend||11-07-2001||02:00 PM||||Before you give up on it though, see if you can demo it in a friends car... try to find someone who has a nice sub that does not require alot of watts.  JL Audio 10w0's come to mind ....<P>Perhaps you can convince a shop to demo your amp with one of their subs ("I want to buy a sub, but I want to make sure it will sound good with my amp").<P>The amount of bump you want is totally personal prefernce, so give it a go!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||DR650SE||11-07-2001||02:49 PM||||Thanks Godsend that reminds me.  I have a small 6.5" sub that I could try it on.  I think I fried the amp on that one cuz it was built in.  It was a small pioneer tube sub.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||11
Z||000007||avengador1||11-07-2001||03:06 PM||||Can you bridge the amp? If you can it will increase the output considerably. You can build a cutoff filter so only low frequency gets thru to the woofer. If you have a free air woofer you don't need a box, but it will sound better with one. Go to Radio Shack and find their book on how to build speaker enclosures. You will learn a lot.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||11-07-2001||06:55 PM||||Also, you don't need to sh!tcan it yet. Although I agree it will do a sorry job with a 10, it will definately give punch to your 4x10s in the dash. Again, not enough to set any SPL records, but an improvement over stock.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||11-07-2001||08:09 PM||||if you just got it and you have the reciept i'd say take it back if they'll take it. tell 'em it's not what you expected or something. not meant to be insulting or anything but...man, just take it back.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fierowrecker||11-08-2001||01:33 AM||||Hey DR!<BR>Check out <A HREF="http://www.partsexpress.com" TARGET=_blank>www.partsexpress.com</A>  for what you want to know...<BR>Even have design data for subs and such!<BR>I built an 8 inch dual voice coil sub box out of 8 inch PVC pipe and plexiglass, and I am running a 125 watt amp filtered at 200 Hz and it provides the thump I was looking for...<BR>Matches the output of my head unit very nicely!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000011||SKIDMARK||11-08-2001||02:02 AM||||Audiovox is great.....if you shop at K-Mart. Really, if you want inexpensive, it will work but you will never be happy with the sound quality. What it boils down to is for the "BIG" sound, you have to spend the big bucks. Check out Crutchfield as mentioned above. Not the best deals in the world but their people know their stuff!<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||13
